"text": "This Roman cup is green, put a candle behind it, and it turns blood red. No paint, no hidden trick, just glass. It's 1600 years old, and for centuries nobody could explain it. Then, scientists finally looked inside it with an electron microscope. You see, the glass is sprinkled with gold and silver, inspects a thousand times thinner than a hair. Light bouncing off them looks green, light shining through them looks red, and nobody knows if the Romans did it on purpose. So 16 centuries ago, someone was doing nanotechnology and might not have even known.",
